From 4dfb4cc1f02a3600eed9bf0541f584e36fb8a254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:19:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: name a stopped sync loop in the stuck
 warning, sync status and create

Incident (MacBook, 2026-11-02 20:47 PT): the gateway logged "kanban sync: not starting: board default: this
core does not declare columns a newer core added (tasks: last_spawn_error, spawn_failures)" once, and its sync
watcher never respun. With sync enabled every claim goes through the Board lease, so the board stalled (52 outbox
ops unpushed, 15 ready, 0 running). Nothing said why: the dispatcher-stuck warning named only claim_deferred /
skipped_ineligible counts, `hermes kanban sync status` printed last_error: None (it reads outbox rows only), and
kanban_create(placement="hub") kept returning local runs_on=[machine:hub] rows that only the stopped loop could
push. The root cause is fixed in #764; this is the detection half, for any future start refusal (a schema-ahead
refusal is legitimate after a core rollback).

- hermes_cli/kanban_sync_runstate.py (new): run_forever records {running: false, since, reason, pid} atomically in
  <kanban home>/kanban/.sync-state.json when it refuses to start (no identity, schema-ahead board), gives the sync
  role up mid-run, stops, or crashes. A completed round clears the file. Readers trust it only while
  kanban.sync.enabled is on.
- stuck_warning: when claims are deferred and the record says sync is down, the line says
  "... and kanban sync not running since <time>: <reason>" instead of pointing at runs_on/placement.
  The dispatcher health JSON (.dispatcher-health.json) has no reason field, so it is unchanged.
- sync status: new "running" row ("no: kanban sync not running since ...: <reason>" / "yes (no stop recorded)").
- kanban_create: while sync is down a machine pin is not rewritten to runs_on; it takes the gateway placement
  route (relay) like any other pin, and an explicit or marker-derived runs_on is refused (sync_not_running)
  naming the sync state. Courier creates are unchanged. Claim behaviour is unchanged.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_schema_guard.py, pre_rename_live + upstream_new_field fixture): a
refused start names the state in the stuck warning and in sync status; a healthy round clears it and the warning
has no sync clause; a loop exit is recorded; the state is ignored with sync off; a machine-pin create while sync is
down returns no runs_on row (placement pin and explicit runs_on) and a pin takes the gateway relay. 7 of them fail
with the production changes reverted.
